course: dictionary
lesson: 1898
title: Colonist: a settler in a new land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A colonist is a noun for a person who goes to live in a new land that is ruled by their home country. You can see the word in both forms: a colonist, and colonists for more than one. Read the clues around it: «The colonists grew angry that Britain taxed them though they had no say in its Parliament.» The colonists were people living far from Britain, but still ruled by it.
explain: In history, colonists are often the first settlers from Europe in places such as America, Australia or New Zealand. Phrases like «early colonists» and «British colonists» tell you who they were and when they came. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word.
explain: The land was not empty. It already belonged to Native peoples, so colonists often took land from them and harmed the people living there. «Under the Spanish encomienda system, colonists were given the right to the labour and tribute of Indigenous people.» Reading history well means asking who was hurt, as well as who arrived.
fact: A colonist is a settler who goes to live in a new land ruled by their home country.
fact: «The colonists» who lived in America in the 1700s were people from Britain, and the land was part of Britain's colonies.
fact: Colonists often took land that already belonged to Native peoples, and many people were harmed.
fact: «Early colonists» means the first settlers to arrive in a place.
fact: In science fiction, «colonists on Mars» are people who would settle a new planet.
exercise: What is a colonist? | A person who only visits a land for a short holiday | A soldier who fights at sea | A ruler who lives in a palace | *A person who settles in a new land ruled by their home country
exercise: In «The colonists grew angry that Britain taxed them», who were the colonists ruled by? | *Britain | The Taíno | Spain | The Moon
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Under the Spanish encomienda system, colonists were given the right to the labour and tribute of Indigenous people.» that means the first people who lived on the land. | system | labour | *Indigenous | colonists
test: Which group were colonists in the thirteen American colonies? | Native Americans who had lived there for thousands of years | Pirates sailing the seas | Tourists visiting for a week | *British people who settled there and were ruled by Britain
test: Why might a history book say colonists harmed people? | *Because they often took land that already belonged to Native peoples | Because they built many schools for children | Because they had no homes at all | Because they always stayed at home
exam: Which sentence uses colonist correctly? | Every colonist wears a red hat to the park | Colonists are people who sing in a choir | The colonists took a bus to school every morning | *The colonists in America were ruled by Britain until they declared independence
